WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.552
SuperEMeans

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:03.309
making e-means clustering

00:00:03.121 --> 00:00:04.536
3x faster

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.673
The SuperKMeans authors

00:00:06.485 --> 00:00:08.041
fused their dimension-pruning

00:00:07.853 --> 00:00:08.548
trick with the

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.787
new 2-epoch e-means

00:00:09.598 --> 00:00:10.400
algorithm

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.027
clustering high-dimensional

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:13.159
embeddings for IVF

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:14.444
vector indexes much

00:00:14.256 --> 00:00:15.706
faster without losing

00:00:15.518 --> 00:00:16.249
quality

00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:19.332
On 5M 1536-d

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.394
OpenAI embeddings

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.858
SuperEMeans took 128

00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:24.533
s versus 203

00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:25.500
s for e-means

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:27.457
232 s for

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:29.781
SuperKMeans and 985

00:00:29.592 --> 00:00:30.936
s for 10-iteration

00:00:30.748 --> 00:00:31.373
Lloyd's

00:00:31.476 --> 00:00:32.325
with the same

00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:34.106
recall100 as e-means

00:00:34.646 --> 00:00:35.471
The index

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.391
We will build

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.452
an IVF index

00:00:37.264 --> 00:00:38.478
with a point-per-cluster

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.398
ratio of 1

00:00:39.221 --> 00:00:39.504
:

00:00:39.316 --> 00:00:40.412
256

00:00:40.589 --> 00:00:42.169
resulting in approximately

00:00:41.981 --> 00:00:43.702
20,000 centroids for

00:00:43.573 --> 00:00:45.495
OpenAI and 40,000

00:00:45.306 --> 00:00:46.344
centroids for the

00:00:46.155 --> 00:00:47.370
Cohere dataset

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:48.924
Full story on

00:00:48.735 --> 00:00:49.631
the dashboard
